{"rowToken":"row_7845525f622c900575e23ae8","verdict":"LEAK","testedDecision":"Choosing the nurse's best reply to the mother requesting a non-essential outdoor wheelchair trip while Client D's sputum AFB smears remain positive in the AIIR.","requiredStageIds":["stage_2"],"unsafeStageIds":["stage_3"],"stageEnumeration":[{"stageId":"stage_1","contribution":"NONANSWERING","evidenceIds":["case.gpt_case_infection_control_clustered_care_01.stage.stage_1.exhibits.0.content.en"],"basis":"The 0730 student gown and hand-hygiene breach in Room 12 has no bearing on the airborne-precautions visitor request for Client D."},{"stageId":"stage_2","contribution":"REQUIRED","evidenceIds":["case.gpt_case_infection_control_clustered_care_01.stage.stage_2.exhibits.0.content.en","case.gpt_case_infection_control_clustered_care_01.stage.stage_2.exhibits.1.content.en"],"basis":"Supplies the 0915 outdoor-trip request from the unmasked mother and the 1130 note that Client D remains smear positive 2+ in the AIIR."},{"stageId":"stage_3","contribution":"UNSAFE","evidenceIds":["case.gpt_case_infection_control_clustered_care_01.stage.stage_3.exhibits.0.content.en","case.gpt_case_infection_control_clustered_care_01.stage.stage_3.exhibits.0.content.zh"],"basis":"The 1300 entry scripts the keyed teaching: no non-essential AIIR exits while smear-positive, surgical mask only for necessary transport, and N95 instruction plus offering for visitors."}],"partEvidenceIds":["case.gpt_case_infection_control_clustered_care_01.part.gpt_case_infection_control_clustered_care_01_q5.stem.en","case.gpt_case_infection_control_clustered_care_01.part.gpt_case_infection_control_clustered_care_01_q5.key","case.gpt_case_infection_control_clustered_care_01.part.gpt_case_infection_control_clustered_care_01_q5.response.options.1.en","case.gpt_case_infection_control_clustered_care_01.part.gpt_case_infection_control_clustered_care_01_q5.rationale.correct.en"],"stageEvidenceIds":["case.gpt_case_infection_control_clustered_care_01.stage.stage_1.exhibits.0.content.en","case.gpt_case_infection_control_clustered_care_01.stage.stage_2.exhibits.0.content.en","case.gpt_case_infection_control_clustered_care_01.stage.stage_2.exhibits.1.content.en","case.gpt_case_infection_control_clustered_care_01.stage.stage_3.exhibits.0.content.en","case.gpt_case_infection_control_clustered_care_01.stage.stage_3.exhibits.0.content.zh"],"locus":{"stageId":"stage_3","evidenceIds":["case.gpt_case_infection_control_clustered_care_01.stage.stage_3.exhibits.0.content.en"],"verbatimSpan":"non-essential trips outside the AIIR are not permitted while smear-positive"},"bilingualRelation":"PARALLEL","reason":"The Stage 2 item asks how to answer the mother, but Stage 3 narrates the nurse delivering that exact teaching, including the transport-only surgical mask and the N95 visitor policy. That reproduces option q5_a nearly verbatim and disposes of the mask and negative-pressure distractors. The Chinese Stage 3 text carries the same three elements, so the leak relation is parallel."}
{"rowToken":"row_5abde0a2a641bcaafdb51e0e","verdict":"NO_LEAK_COMPLETE_RECORD","testedDecision":"Selecting evaluation and anticipatory-guidance statements at the five-week follow-up showing partial response to sertraline plus CBT in postpartum depression.","requiredStageIds":["stage_1_intake","stage_2_follow_up","stage_3_response"],"unsafeStageIds":[],"stageEnumeration":[{"stageId":"stage_1_intake","contribution":"REQUIRED","evidenceIds":["case.opus22_case_postpartum_intrusive_thoughts_01.stage.stage_1_intake.exhibits.0.content.en"],"basis":"Sets the on-treatment baseline of EPDS 20 and 2-3 fragmented sleep hours against which the option about meaningful improvement is judged."},{"stageId":"stage_2_follow_up","contribution":"REQUIRED","evidenceIds":["case.opus22_case_postpartum_intrusive_thoughts_01.stage.stage_2_follow_up.exhibits.0.content.en"],"basis":"Documents avoidance of bathing the infant alone, nightly breathing checks, PHQ-9 16 and EPDS 18, which give the Stage 3 bathing and score changes their meaning."},{"stageId":"stage_3_response","contribution":"REQUIRED","evidenceIds":["case.opus22_case_postpartum_intrusive_thoughts_01.stage.stage_3_response.exhibits.0.content.en"],"basis":"Supplies EPDS 11, PHQ-9 10, restored sleep and function, and the client's questions about medication duration, breastfeeding safety, and recurrence risk."}],"partEvidenceIds":["case.opus22_case_postpartum_intrusive_thoughts_01.part.opus22_case_postpartum_intrusive_thoughts_01_q5.stem.en","case.opus22_case_postpartum_intrusive_thoughts_01.part.opus22_case_postpartum_intrusive_thoughts_01_q5.key","case.opus22_case_postpartum_intrusive_thoughts_01.part.opus22_case_postpartum_intrusive_thoughts_01_q5.response.options.3.en","case.opus22_case_postpartum_intrusive_thoughts_01.part.opus22_case_postpartum_intrusive_thoughts_01_q5.rationale.correct.en"],"stageEvidenceIds":["case.opus22_case_postpartum_intrusive_thoughts_01.stage.stage_1_intake.exhibits.0.content.en","case.opus22_case_postpartum_intrusive_thoughts_01.stage.stage_2_follow_up.exhibits.0.content.en","case.opus22_case_postpartum_intrusive_thoughts_01.stage.stage_3_response.exhibits.0.content.en"],"locus":{"stageId":null,"evidenceIds":[],"verbatimSpan":null},"bilingualRelation":"PARALLEL","reason":"The item evaluates treatment response, and the keyed statement about improvement across sleep, appetite, function, scores, and infant care is only verifiable by comparing the Stage 1 and Stage 2 trajectory with Stage 3 values. The strongest cue is the Stage 3 note that labeling thoughts as just thoughts is helpful, which points toward continuing CBT, but that lies inside the authored evaluation stage and does not settle the breastfeeding, duration, or recurrence teaching. English and Chinese stages carry the same trajectory data."}
{"rowToken":"row_98a47fe21352505243331d62","verdict":"NO_LEAK_NONANSWERING_DATA","testedDecision":"Choosing what the nurse tells the returning partner who asks why the prenatal visit took so long, without revealing the IPV disclosure.","requiredStageIds":["stage1_private_screening","stage3_safety_plan_and_exit"],"unsafeStageIds":[],"stageEnumeration":[{"stageId":"stage1_private_screening","contribution":"REQUIRED","evidenceIds":["case.opus27_case_ipv_prenatal_care_01.stage.stage1_private_screening.exhibits.0.content.en"],"basis":"Establishes the disclosure and the client's plea that the partner not learn she spoke, which defines what the reply must conceal."},{"stageId":"stage2_safety_discussion","contribution":"NONANSWERING","evidenceIds":["case.opus27_case_ipv_prenatal_care_01.stage.stage2_safety_discussion.exhibits.0.content.en"],"basis":"Financial control, phone monitoring, and custody threats deepen risk context but do not discriminate among the four scripted replies to the partner."},{"stageId":"stage3_safety_plan_and_exit","contribution":"REQUIRED","evidenceIds":["case.opus27_case_ipv_prenatal_care_01.stage.stage3_safety_plan_and_exit.exhibits.0.content.en"],"basis":"Contains the partner's return, the question about the visit length, and the client looking to the nurse, which is the exact moment being answered."}],"partEvidenceIds":["case.opus27_case_ipv_prenatal_care_01.part.opus27_case_ipv_prenatal_care_01_q6.stem.en","case.opus27_case_ipv_prenatal_care_01.part.opus27_case_ipv_prenatal_care_01_q6.key","case.opus27_case_ipv_prenatal_care_01.part.opus27_case_ipv_prenatal_care_01_q6.response.options.1.en","case.opus27_case_ipv_prenatal_care_01.part.opus27_case_ipv_prenatal_care_01_q6.rationale.correct.en"],"stageEvidenceIds":["case.opus27_case_ipv_prenatal_care_01.stage.stage1_private_screening.exhibits.0.content.en","case.opus27_case_ipv_prenatal_care_01.stage.stage2_safety_discussion.exhibits.0.content.en","case.opus27_case_ipv_prenatal_care_01.stage.stage3_safety_plan_and_exit.exhibits.0.content.en"],"locus":{"stageId":null,"evidenceIds":[],"verbatimSpan":null},"bilingualRelation":"PARALLEL","reason":"The strongest extra cue is the Stage 2 catalogue of coercive control, which raises the stakes but never indicates whether the nurse should give a routine visit summary, disclose the bruise discussion, or fabricate a blood pressure crisis. No stage models a reply to the partner, so the candidate must still weigh truthfulness against non-revelation. Both language versions expose the same Stage 2 content."}
{"rowToken":"row_8004d58d098a7f875df3fef3","verdict":"NO_LEAK_NONANSWERING_DATA","testedDecision":"Interpreting new mild bilateral ankle edema with clear lungs at 60 hours and choosing continued assessment and reporting over diuretics or stopping meals.","requiredStageIds":["stage_60h"],"unsafeStageIds":[],"stageEnumeration":[{"stageId":"stage_18h","contribution":"NONANSWERING","evidenceIds":["case.opus26_case_refeeding_syndrome_01.stage.stage_18h.exhibits.0.content.en"],"basis":"The 12-hour phosphorus fall to 2.4 mg/dL and post-meal bloating precede the edema and do not decide between diuresis and monitoring."},{"stageId":"stage_36h","contribution":"NONANSWERING","evidenceIds":["case.opus26_case_refeeding_syndrome_01.stage.stage_36h.exhibits.0.content.en"],"basis":"The 0.8 kg gain and QTc 480 ms document earlier instability, but the stem itself supplies the cumulative 1.1 kg gain and current clear lungs."},{"stageId":"stage_60h","contribution":"REQUIRED","evidenceIds":["case.opus26_case_refeeding_syndrome_01.stage.stage_60h.exhibits.0.content.en"],"basis":"Provides the corrected electrolytes, normal sinus rhythm, clear lungs, weight 40.9 kg, and the new 1+ ankle edema being interpreted."}],"partEvidenceIds":["case.opus26_case_refeeding_syndrome_01.part.opus26_case_refeeding_syndrome_01_q5.stem.en","case.opus26_case_refeeding_syndrome_01.part.opus26_case_refeeding_syndrome_01_q5.key","case.opus26_case_refeeding_syndrome_01.part.opus26_case_refeeding_syndrome_01_q5.response.options.2.en","case.opus26_case_refeeding_syndrome_01.part.opus26_case_refeeding_syndrome_01_q5.rationale.correct.en"],"stageEvidenceIds":["case.opus26_case_refeeding_syndrome_01.stage.stage_18h.exhibits.0.content.en","case.opus26_case_refeeding_syndrome_01.stage.stage_36h.exhibits.0.content.en","case.opus26_case_refeeding_syndrome_01.stage.stage_60h.exhibits.0.content.en"],"locus":{"stageId":null,"evidenceIds":[],"verbatimSpan":null},"bilingualRelation":"PARALLEL","reason":"The strongest extra cue is the Stage 2 weight gain of 0.8 kg in under 36 hours, which fits a fluid-retention pattern, but it does not state that the ankle edema is expected refeeding edema or that diuretics should be avoided. No earlier stage frames edema management, so the interpretation still rests on the Stage 3 respiratory and electrolyte picture. The Chinese stages contain the same values."}
{"rowToken":"row_4ca84de5c7efa6aad8ced3ac","verdict":"NO_LEAK_COMPLETE_RECORD","testedDecision":"Ranking which identified breach posed the greatest cross-contamination risk to other unit clients when the charge nurse asks at 1230.","requiredStageIds":["stage_1","stage_2","stage_3"],"unsafeStageIds":[],"stageEnumeration":[{"stageId":"stage_1","contribution":"REQUIRED","evidenceIds":["case.gpt_case_infection_control_clustered_care_01.stage.stage_1.exhibits.0.content.en"],"basis":"Supplies the bare-hand door-handle contamination option and the targeted disinfection already arranged at that single doorway."},{"stageId":"stage_2","contribution":"REQUIRED","evidenceIds":["case.gpt_case_infection_control_clustered_care_01.stage.stage_2.exhibits.0.content.en"],"basis":"Supplies three option stems: the dedicated stethoscope on the clean-utility counter next to the clean supply cart, the standard linen bag error, and Client B's wife at the doorway."},{"stageId":"stage_3","contribution":"REQUIRED","evidenceIds":["case.gpt_case_infection_control_clustered_care_01.stage.stage_3.exhibits.0.content.en"],"basis":"Holds the 1215 debrief listing the identified breaches and the 1230 charge-nurse question that this item reproduces."}],"partEvidenceIds":["case.gpt_case_infection_control_clustered_care_01.part.gpt_case_infection_control_clustered_care_01_q4.stem.en","case.gpt_case_infection_control_clustered_care_01.part.gpt_case_infection_control_clustered_care_01_q4.key","case.gpt_case_infection_control_clustered_care_01.part.gpt_case_infection_control_clustered_care_01_q4.response.options.3.en","case.gpt_case_infection_control_clustered_care_01.part.gpt_case_infection_control_clustered_care_01_q4.rationale.correct.en"],"stageEvidenceIds":["case.gpt_case_infection_control_clustered_care_01.stage.stage_1.exhibits.0.content.en","case.gpt_case_infection_control_clustered_care_01.stage.stage_2.exhibits.0.content.en","case.gpt_case_infection_control_clustered_care_01.stage.stage_3.exhibits.0.content.en"],"locus":{"stageId":null,"evidenceIds":[],"verbatimSpan":null},"bilingualRelation":"PARALLEL","reason":"The stem is explicitly the 1230 charge-nurse question inside Stage 3, and the four options map onto breaches distributed across Stages 1 and 2, so the item is authored on the assembled record. The strongest cue is the end-of-shift stethoscope remediation describing disinfection of clean-utility surfaces and removal of nearby supplies, but that restates the exposure pathway already given in Stage 2 and sits in the item's own stage. The Chinese record mirrors the same distribution."}
{"rowToken":"row_5cd98045ae8eda3459ace03a","verdict":"NO_LEAK_NONANSWERING_DATA","testedDecision":"Selecting documentation and communication actions after the client asks whether her IPV disclosure enters the chart and whether her partner can see it.","requiredStageIds":["stage2_safety_discussion","stage3_safety_plan_and_exit"],"unsafeStageIds":[],"stageEnumeration":[{"stageId":"stage1_private_screening","contribution":"NONANSWERING","evidenceIds":["case.opus27_case_ipv_prenatal_care_01.stage.stage1_private_screening.exhibits.0.content.en"],"basis":"The verbatim disclosure and secrecy request explain why confidentiality matters but identify no portal, proxy, device, or contact-method safeguard."},{"stageId":"stage2_safety_discussion","contribution":"REQUIRED","evidenceIds":["case.opus27_case_ipv_prenatal_care_01.stage.stage2_safety_discussion.exhibits.0.content.en"],"basis":"States that the partner monitors her phone and that the disclosure was already documented in the client's own words, grounding the documentation and access-risk options."},{"stageId":"stage3_safety_plan_and_exit","contribution":"REQUIRED","evidenceIds":["case.opus27_case_ipv_prenatal_care_01.stage.stage3_safety_plan_and_exit.exhibits.0.content.en"],"basis":"Contains the chart and partner-access question, the secondary phone number, the safe-contact check before sending messages, and the discreet resource card."}],"partEvidenceIds":["case.opus27_case_ipv_prenatal_care_01.part.opus27_case_ipv_prenatal_care_01_q5.stem.en","case.opus27_case_ipv_prenatal_care_01.part.opus27_case_ipv_prenatal_care_01_q5.key","case.opus27_case_ipv_prenatal_care_01.part.opus27_case_ipv_prenatal_care_01_q5.response.options.1.en","case.opus27_case_ipv_prenatal_care_01.part.opus27_case_ipv_prenatal_care_01_q5.rationale.correct.en"],"stageEvidenceIds":["case.opus27_case_ipv_prenatal_care_01.stage.stage1_private_screening.exhibits.0.content.en","case.opus27_case_ipv_prenatal_care_01.stage.stage2_safety_discussion.exhibits.0.content.en","case.opus27_case_ipv_prenatal_care_01.stage.stage3_safety_plan_and_exit.exhibits.0.content.en"],"locus":{"stageId":null,"evidenceIds":[],"verbatimSpan":null},"bilingualRelation":"PARALLEL","reason":"The only surplus stage is Stage 1, whose plea not to tell the partner mildly discourages an unsafe voicemail, yet the voicemail and portal distractors are already excluded by the monitored-phone and secondary-number facts the item legitimately uses. Stage 1 adds no guidance on documentation wording or proxy-access screening. The Chinese Stage 1 text carries the same limited cue."}
{"rowToken":"row_f72f76b189d83d03b1b52e5a","verdict":"NO_LEAK_NONANSWERING_DATA","testedDecision":"Deciding the nurse's action before giving potassium chloride 20 mEq in 100 mL over one hour through a peripheral line.","requiredStageIds":["stage_2"],"unsafeStageIds":[],"stageEnumeration":[{"stageId":"stage_1","contribution":"NONANSWERING","evidenceIds":["case.opus_case_lithium_toxicity_01.stage.stage_1.exhibits.0.content.en"],"basis":"The 0930 vomiting, neurologic decline, and saline orders precede the potassium order and say nothing about peripheral concentration limits."},{"stageId":"stage_2","contribution":"REQUIRED","evidenceIds":["case.opus_case_lithium_toxicity_01.stage.stage_2.exhibits.0.content.en"],"basis":"Contains the potassium chloride 20 mEq in 100 mL peripheral pump order whose concentration and rate the nurse must verify before administering."},{"stageId":"stage_3","contribution":"NONANSWERING","evidenceIds":["case.opus_case_lithium_toxicity_01.stage.stage_3.exhibits.0.content.en"],"basis":"Post-dialysis potassium 3.8 mEq/L shows eventual repletion but never records whether the infusion was held, clarified, or given as written."}],"partEvidenceIds":["case.opus_case_lithium_toxicity_01.part.opus_case_lithium_toxicity_q4.stem.en","case.opus_case_lithium_toxicity_01.part.opus_case_lithium_toxicity_q4.key","case.opus_case_lithium_toxicity_01.part.opus_case_lithium_toxicity_q4.response.options.2.en","case.opus_case_lithium_toxicity_01.part.opus_case_lithium_toxicity_q4.rationale.correct.en"],"stageEvidenceIds":["case.opus_case_lithium_toxicity_01.stage.stage_1.exhibits.0.content.en","case.opus_case_lithium_toxicity_01.stage.stage_2.exhibits.0.content.en","case.opus_case_lithium_toxicity_01.stage.stage_3.exhibits.0.content.en"],"locus":{"stageId":null,"evidenceIds":[],"verbatimSpan":null},"bilingualRelation":"PARALLEL","reason":"The strongest exposed cue is the Stage 3 normalization of potassium to 3.8 mEq/L, which merely confirms repletion happened at some point and does not disclose whether the nurse questioned the 20 mEq per 100 mL concentration. The keyed hold-and-clarify judgment still depends on comparing the Stage 2 order against peripheral potassium limits. Both languages present the same order and outcome."}
{"rowToken":"row_68150776d6a7366265be7daf","verdict":"LEAK","testedDecision":"Selecting nursing responses when the tearful client blames the food, asks to stop eating, and is observed hiding food during supervised refeeding.","requiredStageIds":["stage_36h"],"unsafeStageIds":["stage_60h"],"stageEnumeration":[{"stageId":"stage_18h","contribution":"NONANSWERING","evidenceIds":["case.opus26_case_refeeding_syndrome_01.stage.stage_18h.exhibits.0.content.en"],"basis":"Earlier food rearranging, pacing, and post-meal bloating describe similar behaviors but not the Stage 2 refusal and napkin hiding being answered."},{"stageId":"stage_36h","contribution":"REQUIRED","evidenceIds":["case.opus26_case_refeeding_syndrome_01.stage.stage_36h.exhibits.0.content.en"],"basis":"Supplies the tearful request to stop eating, the observed food hiding with sitter intervention, and the held caloric advancement that frame the response set."},{"stageId":"stage_60h","contribution":"UNSAFE","evidenceIds":["case.opus26_case_refeeding_syndrome_01.stage.stage_60h.exhibits.0.content.en","case.opus26_case_refeeding_syndrome_01.stage.stage_60h.exhibits.0.content.zh"],"basis":"Reports that intake stayed at 1,200 kcal and that supportive counseling left her calmer and eating 75 percent, which eliminates the stop-meals option and endorses validation with reassurance."}],"partEvidenceIds":["case.opus26_case_refeeding_syndrome_01.part.opus26_case_refeeding_syndrome_01_q4.stem.en","case.opus26_case_refeeding_syndrome_01.part.opus26_case_refeeding_syndrome_01_q4.key","case.opus26_case_refeeding_syndrome_01.part.opus26_case_refeeding_syndrome_01_q4.response.options.3.en","case.opus26_case_refeeding_syndrome_01.part.opus26_case_refeeding_syndrome_01_q4.rationale.byChoice.3.en"],"stageEvidenceIds":["case.opus26_case_refeeding_syndrome_01.stage.stage_18h.exhibits.0.content.en","case.opus26_case_refeeding_syndrome_01.stage.stage_36h.exhibits.0.content.en","case.opus26_case_refeeding_syndrome_01.stage.stage_60h.exhibits.0.content.en","case.opus26_case_refeeding_syndrome_01.stage.stage_60h.exhibits.0.content.zh"],"locus":{"stageId":"stage_60h","evidenceIds":["case.opus26_case_refeeding_syndrome_01.stage.stage_60h.exhibits.0.content.en"],"verbatimSpan":"After supportive counseling from the psychiatric liaison team, the client is calmer and is eating about 75% of offered food."},"bilingualRelation":"PARALLEL","reason":"Stage 3 shows the outcome of the very decision being tested: meals were maintained at the ordered calories and supportive counseling produced improved intake, which directly discards the keyed distractor of agreeing to stop meals and validates the calm, factual, empathic approach. That is more than a later timestamp, because it reports the result of the candidate's choice. The Chinese Stage 3 sentence states the same counseling outcome and continued calorie level."}
{"rowToken":"row_00356840fde1acb28b4193a9","verdict":"NO_LEAK_NONANSWERING_DATA","testedDecision":"Distinguishing six-hour findings that still block discharge to the same home from findings that only show response to emergency treatment.","requiredStageIds":["stage_2_ed_initial","stage_3_six_hours_ed"],"unsafeStageIds":[],"stageEnumeration":[{"stageId":"stage_1_home_visit_action","contribution":"NONANSWERING","evidenceIds":["case.opus24_case_elder_neglect_med_mismanagement_01.stage.stage_1_home_visit_action.exhibits.0.content.en"],"basis":"The escalation and mandatory reporting initiation explain how the APS referral began, but Stage 3 already states the referral and care conference remain unresolved."},{"stageId":"stage_2_ed_initial","contribution":"REQUIRED","evidenceIds":["case.opus24_case_elder_neglect_med_mismanagement_01.stage.stage_2_ed_initial.exhibits.0.content.en"],"basis":"Documents the pre-treatment U waves, prolonged QT, bradycardia, and hypotension that let the Stage 3 changes be read as response rather than resolution."},{"stageId":"stage_3_six_hours_ed","contribution":"REQUIRED","evidenceIds":["case.opus24_case_elder_neglect_med_mismanagement_01.stage.stage_3_six_hours_ed.exhibits.0.content.en"],"basis":"Provides potassium 3.4, creatinine 1.6 above the 1.2 baseline, the worsened sacral wound, improved vitals and rhythm, and the pending APS and discharge conference."}],"partEvidenceIds":["case.opus24_case_elder_neglect_med_mismanagement_01.part.opus24_case_elder_neglect_med_mismanagement_01_q6.stem.en","case.opus24_case_elder_neglect_med_mismanagement_01.part.opus24_case_elder_neglect_med_mismanagement_01_q6.key","case.opus24_case_elder_neglect_med_mismanagement_01.part.opus24_case_elder_neglect_med_mismanagement_01_q6.response.options.2.en","case.opus24_case_elder_neglect_med_mismanagement_01.part.opus24_case_elder_neglect_med_mismanagement_01_q6.rationale.correct.en"],"stageEvidenceIds":["case.opus24_case_elder_neglect_med_mismanagement_01.stage.sta